{"format":"floorplan/1","building":"POWELL","floor":"2","title":"Powell Library floor 2","extent":"full","source":{"publisher":"UCLA Library","what":"\"Powell Library Building Floorplans\" (color vector PDF, all four floors on one sheet with room numbers; taken down since, recovered from the Common Crawl 2018-03 capture)","url":"https://www.library.ucla.edu/sites/default/files/Powell-floorplan-color_link_0.pdf","file":"https://www.library.ucla.edu/sites/default/files/Powell-floorplan-color_link_0.pdf","archive":"Common Crawl CC-MAIN-2018-13, captured 2018-03-20","date":"undated, online 2018-03","accessed":"2026-10-15"},"how":"Walls are the plan's own vector lines (from the PDF), rooms are the spaces they enclose, and room numbers are the PDF's text. The plan was fitted to the ground with a similarity transform on 8 control points (outer corner of the east wing's south end (plan top left; the plan is drawn south up); inner corner of the east wing's south end; inner corner of the west wing's south end; outer corner of the west wing's south end (plan top right); north-east corner of the building (plan bottom left); north-west corner of the building (plan bottom right); jog in the east wall where the wider north block starts; jog in the west wall where the wider north block starts).","notes":["Traced from the Second Floor (top left) of the UCLA Library sheet.","The sheet is drawn south up (its compass has E on the left and W on the right); UCLA's main entrance is on the north face and the plan's Main Entrance is at the bottom, so the plan is turned 180 degrees. The fit uses the outer wall corners of the two wings and of the wider north block against the building outline.","Elevators are the gray boxes with the up/down glyph and stairs the hatched boxes (both from the sheet's legend); they are added as hand-placed boxes at the sheet's positions. Restroom icons (legend: Restrooms) set the kind of the room holding them.","The sheet leaves openings in the outer wall of the 